            <ArticleTitle>Coarctation of the aorta diagnosed by cardiac computed tomography angiography in a 49-year-old man presenting with acute myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>655-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10554-015-0808-6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aortic coarctation in patients with acute myocardial infarction is an uncommon finding, We report the case of a 49-year-old man with acute myocardial infarction and diagnosis of severe aortic coarctation in concomitance with a three-dimensional computed tomography scan.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
